module Main
import Base

-- Boolean prims (&&, ||) over dynamically-allocated boxed Bools. Bool is the
-- nullary constructor True/False, so every `True`/`False` here allocates a fresh
-- heap cell (RVBox). The Perceus pass moves these owned operand cells INTO the
-- boolOp prim, which must DROP both operands while allocating its fresh result.
-- Without that drop the operand cells leak (Suite B: stLive > baseline). Two
-- nested ops chain a freshly-allocated result back into a second op, so both the
-- literal operands and the intermediate result are exercised as owned moves.
main = (True && False) || True
